From 5f08dcaf99587e8674f1d0390387283b7158b11c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: oms004 <ricekent@163.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 08:45:35 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] fix(herdr-fleet): distinguish PR query failure from no PR
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

pr_info returned None for both "no PR" and every query failure, so a
failed gh pr list (e.g. a non-GitHub remote like the Gitee host in
issue #39) was reported as pr=null and next_step still suggested
submitting a PR.

pr_info now returns a tri-state: found / none / unknown with an error
summary. Only a successful query with an empty array is none; non-zero
exit, OSError, timeout, invalid JSON and structurally unexpected JSON
are all unknown. status --json keeps repos.<key>.pr (the PR object when
found, else null) and adds pr_state and pr_error; text shows
"PR: #12 ..." / "PR: 无" / "PR: 未知（查询失败：…）". When any repo is
unknown, next_step requires manually checking whether a PR exists
instead of unconditionally suggesting one, while keeping more urgent
advice like blocked. Notices mark unknown with "?", kept alongside
found links in mixed-repository tasks; "-" now means confirmed absent.

FLEET_GH keeps working as the provider adapter entry point; workflow.md
documents its contract (same gh pr list arguments, same JSON array,
non-zero exit with stderr on failure).

Generated with [Devin](https://devin.ai)

Co-Authored-By: Devin <158243242+devin-ai-integration[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>
