From 210680a1228e1001fdd70e59d4456ddbed5da717 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: oms004 <ricekent@163.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 09:19:50 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] fix(herdr-fleet): supersede stale-round done/idle notices
 on new round
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A queued done/idle event could be delivered to the coordinator after a
new working round had already started, presenting the old round's
terminal as if the task had just finished (issue #38).

Each inbox event now records the round baseline that produced it (same
value the dedup_key has always embedded; older records are read through
the key). When a new round is established — a confirmed send/new
submission, or a manual working edge — pending done/idle events of
older rounds for that task are marked superseded: kept in inbox --all,
attempts untouched, never prompted. Failed submissions supersede
nothing; blocked/exited events are never auto-superseded.

Delivery builds the notice outside locks as before, then re-checks
inside the delivery lock plus the involved task locks (acquired in
slug order): pending membership and each done/idle event's baseline
against the task's current TASK.md round. The re-check and the prompt
run under the same task locks so a send cannot slip between them;
the cross-task state lock is still never held during external calls.

Stale blocked events are still delivered but annotated with the event
round, the current round and the live agent status
([round old -> new] 当前状态 working); the phase is derived from the
live status rather than the recorded terminal. Every notice line now
carries round information; rounds that cannot be determined show
[round ?] instead of implying a fresh terminal.

Fixes #38

