From 85f585e75e005c8c88726191eac939980850d96b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: oms004 <ricekent@163.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 09:28:18 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] fix(herdr-fleet): rebuild notice when round drifts during
 construction

The locked recheck only compared pending-set membership and done/idle
baselines, so a still-pending blocked event kept its construction-time
"[round N]" text even after a send established a newer round in the
window. Re-verify the per-task round snapshot used to build the notice
inside the delivery+task locks; on drift, rebuild the message outside
the locks so blocked/exited lines carry "[round N -> M]" with the live
agent status. Also scope the global-lock wording in workflow.md to the
delivery path (task_event still calls agent get under the state lock).

